# Rule 2 — Per-filter scan + apply, stop near 30 processed

**Session ceiling:** stop when `applied + skipped >= 30` (already-applied / company-site count as skipped).

- Shuffle **titles, keywords, and locations** each session — do not always start with the first preference chip.
- For **one** title/keyword search at a time:
  - Keep Naukri sidebar filters (salary / work mode / cities) via All Filters.
  - Scroll and **auto next-page** this list. **Never ask** the user to click “Next page”.
  - Then **apply** that filter’s matches (short settle, job → next job).
  - If the list is thin, still apply every match found — do not block on a full 30 for that search.
- Then switch to another random title/keyword (sidebar filters stay) and repeat.
- Do **not** start another search once `applied + skipped >= 30`.
- Cap each filter’s queue to the remaining room (`30 - processed`) so one fat search cannot queue 80 jobs.
- If a search matches 0, skip apply and try the next title/keyword.
- If the whole plan matches 0, do not apply; report that nothing matched.
- When the session finishes, ask **Apply more** or **Close — view dashboard**. Close must close the Naukri work tab and open the Cosmo dashboard (reuse an existing Cosmo tab when possible). Do not prompt for another Next page.
- Never invent extra result pages past real pagination.
- Single Naukri work tab only.
